quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  6,158,"Are they waiting for the (very) angels to come to them, or your Lord to come (Himself), or some (special) signs of your Lord to come? The day when some (special) signs of your Lord do come, belief shall not benefit any soul that did not believe beforehand and did not earn some goodness in its belief. Say: ‘Wait! We (too) are waiting.’"
  6,159,"Indeed, those who split up their religion and become sects, you have nothing to do with them. Their case rests only with Allah. Then, He will inform them about what they used to do."
  6,160,"Whoever brings a good deed shall receive ten times the like of it, and whoever brings an evil deed shall not be recompensed except the like of it. And they shall not be wronged."
  6,161,"Say: ‘Indeed, my Lord has guided me to a straight path, the upright religion, the religion of Ibrahim (Abraham), the man of pure faith. And he was not among the polytheists.’"
  6,162,"Say: ‘Indeed my prayer, my ritual sacrifices, my life and my death are (all) for Allah, the Lord of all worlds."
  6,163,"He has no partner, and that is what I have been commanded (to follow). I am the first of those who submit (to Allah).’"
  6,164,"Say: ‘Shall I seek a Lord other than Allah, while He is the Lord of everything?’ No soul commits evil but against itself, and no bearer shall bear the burden of another. Then, to your Lord is your (ultimate) return. And He will inform you regarding that over which you used to differ.’"
  6,165,"He is the One Who made you successors on the earth and raised some of you in ranks above others, so He may test you regarding what He has given you (as a trust). Indeed, your Lord is Swift in retribution. And indeed, He is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
